WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.510
You flip a coin ten times.

2
00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:07.770
Heads, heads, tails, heads, heads,
heads, tails, heads, tails,

3
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:08.420
heads.

4
00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.870
That's seven heads out of ten.

5
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:13.530
Your friend says the
coin must be unfair.

6
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.910
Is your friend right?

7
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.990
Can ten flips prove
that a coin is biased?

8
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:20.810
In this mission, you'll find
a probability by doing an

9
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:23.930
experiment, like dropping a
drawing pin again and again,

10
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:25.380
and counting the results.

11
00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:28.650
You'll compare experimental
and theoretical probability.

12
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:32.670
And you'll use a probability
to predict how often something

13
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.930
should happen.

14
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:38.330
Your mission: decide what ten
coin flips can really tell you.
